<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hrodgaud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 776</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Rotgaud of Friuli, Hrodgaud of Friuli, Rotgaud</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hrodgaud was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friuli">Friuli</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> conquered the Lombard Kingdom in 774 he kept his duchy, but in 776 he rebelled, hoping to restore Lombard rule with the help of other dukes. Charlemagne crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, Hrodgaud was killed in battle, and Friuli was given to Frankish counts.</p></div>
